  "result": "Six of the 19 purchased Components have less stock on hand, summed across all locations, than their safety stock level. All six have a safety stock level of 500.\n\n| Product number | Total on hand | Shortest average vendor lead time (days) |\n|---|---|---|\n| SE-M798 | 422 | 15 |\n| SE-M940 | 355 | 17 |\n| SE-R995 | 467 | 15 |\n| SE-T762 | 402 | 15 |\n| PD-R347 | 498 | 16 |\n| PD-R563 | 494 | 16 |\n\nThe warehouse and purchasing systems write item codes differently from the product list. Warehouse codes start with \"AW:\" and vendor codes use underscores instead of hyphens, so I converted both to match product numbers. Every purchased Component had warehouse stock records, so none were left out. The lead times count every vendor that lists the item, whether or not the vendor is active.",
